    "sentence_translations": [
      "Don't Casually Use 2B",
      "",
      "If an English text message says “2B or not 2B” a lot of people will only think it is short for “to be or not to be”.",
      "But if you send this text message to a Chinese friend, you should avoid using this abbreviation.",
      "Why?",
      "Because in China, 2B means “idiot” and is used to scold people.",
      "So when Chinese people see “2B”, the first thing that comes to mind is certainly not “to be”.",
      "Instead they will think you are scolding them.",
      "",
      "2B can also be written “èr bī” and is originally internet slang, but is now a popular catchphrase for many people.",
      "There is also the word “shǎ bī” which has a similar meaning.",
      "Even though sometimes these can be used for teasing between very close friends, ..",
      ".. most of the time it is used to berate people, so you should not abuse it.",
      ""
    ]
